Package: paradoxR
Title: Colour Palettes for 'ggplot2' and Faster 'Bioconductor' Analysis
Version: 26.11.1
Authors@R: 
    person("catch-26", email = "59668327+catch-26@users.noreply.github.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides drop-in replacements for the default colour scales of
    'ggplot2', with discrete, continuous, binned, ordinal and diverging scales and one
    switch for every plot. Also makes 'clusterProfiler', 'GOSemSim', 'DESeq2'
    and 'sva' faster when loaded: GO and KEGG data are cached on disk, and
    slow internal steps are replaced by vectorised code. Stores the results of
    slow 'Seurat', 'Signac', 'DiffBind', 'csaw', 'GenomicAlignments',
    'ChIPseeker', 'EnrichedHeatmap', 'GSVA', 'sva', 'DESeq2', 'stats' and
    'MASS' steps and reuses them when the data, input
    files, arguments and package versions are unchanged; unused cache entries
    expire after 7 days. Results are identical to the original functions.
